course: dictionary
lesson: 9772
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A surfer is a person who rides waves on a surfboard. Look at the words around surfer to check its meaning. In the beach story, a surfer helps rescue a father who has been swept out, so you can picture the sea.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Surfer can also mean a person who uses the internet a lot, as in «a web surfer». Read the clues: is the text about water, or about a screen? The words around the word tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «A keen surfer» means someone who loves surfing, and the sentence still makes sense with that meaning.
fact: Surfer means a person who rides waves on a surfboard.
fact: A surfer can also be a person who uses the internet a lot, as in «a web surfer».
fact: Surfers ride the waves in places such as Australia, New Zealand, California and Hawaii.
fact: «The pororoca» is a tidal wave that pushes up the mouth of the Amazon, and surfers have ridden it for over thirty minutes.
fact: In beach safety, surfers must stay out of the flags area for swimmers and must know about rip currents.
exercise: «A family in Australia swam where the water looked calm; it was a rip, and a surfer had to rescue the father.» What does surfer mean in this sentence? | A flag that shows where to swim | *A person who rides waves on a surfboard | A person who uses the internet a lot | A fish that lives near the shore
exercise: Ravi reads «a web surfer» and asks what it means. Which answer is right? | A rip current in the sea | A wave that pushes up a river | *A person who uses the internet a lot | A person who rides waves on a surfboard
exercise: Which word in «surfers have ridden it for over thirty minutes» tells you the surfers are riding on water? | minutes | thirty | *ridden | surfers
test: Tom says a surfer is a type of fish. What is a surfer? | A safety flag on the beach | A type of fish | A tidal wave in a river | *A person who rides waves on a surfboard
test: «She is a web surfer.» What does surfer mean in this sentence? | A person who rides waves on a surfboard | A wave pushing up a river | *A person who uses the internet a lot | A flag that marks the swimming area
exam: Jayden reads about surfers and asks which fact is true. Which sentence is true? | *Surfers must stay out of the flags area for swimmers | A surfer is a type of bird that lives on the beach | A surfer always uses the internet to ride waves | Surfers can only ride waves in the Amazon
